{
  "dom_id": "step-q183426",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the missing values in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| {{field-1}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-2}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-3}} | $B⇒A$ |\n| {{field-4}} | $A⇒B$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"If $A,$ then $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$A$ only if $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$A$ if $B$\" means $B⇒A$\n\n- \"$A$ implies $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| If $A,$ then $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A$ only if $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A$ if $B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $A$ implies $B$ | $A⇒B$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
